## 🚀 Quick Start (Copy-Paste Commands)

### 1️⃣ Database Setup

```bash
# Create database and user
sudo -u postgres psql << 'EOF'
CREATE DATABASE sugarcane_harvest;
CREATE USER sugarcane_user WITH PASSWORD 'secure_password_123';
GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON DATABASE sugarcane_harvest TO sugarcane_user;
ALTER DATABASE sugarcane_harvest OWNER TO sugarcane_user;
\q
EOF

# Initialize schema
psql -U sugarcane_user -d sugarcane_harvest -f schema.sql
```

**Test Database:**
```bash
psql -U sugarcane_user -d sugarcane_harvest -c "SELECT * FROM users;"
```

---

### 2️⃣ Backend Setup

```bash
# Create project directory
mkdir -p sugarcane_harvesting/backend
cd sugarcane_harvesting/backend

# Create virtual environment
python3 -m venv venv

# Activate venv (Linux/Mac)
source venv/bin/activate

# Activate venv (Windows)
venv\Scripts\activate

# Install dependencies
pip install Flask flask-cors psycopg2-binary APScheduler

# Or use requirements.txt
cat > requirements.txt << 'EOF'
Flask==3.0.0
flask-cors==4.0.0
psycopg2-binary==2.9.9
APScheduler==3.10.4
EOF

pip install -r requirements.txt
```

---

### 3️⃣ Frontend Setup

```bash
# Create frontend directory
mkdir -p ../frontend
cd ../frontend

# Copy the index.html file to this directory
# (Use the React frontend artifact provided above)
```

---

### 4️⃣ Run the System

**Terminal 1 - Backend:**
```bash
cd sugarcane_harvesting/backend
source venv/bin/activate  # Windows: venv\Scripts\activate
python app.py
```

**Expected Output:**
```
======================================================================
🚀 Sugarcane Harvesting System - Full Stack Backend
======================================================================
✓ Database pool created
✓ Scheduler started
✓ Flask starting on http://0.0.0.0:5000
======================================================================

 * Running on http://0.0.0.0:5000
```

**Terminal 2 - Frontend:**
```bash
cd sugarcane_harvesting/frontend

# Option 1: Python HTTP Server
python -m http.server 3000

# Option 2: Node.js HTTP Server (if you have Node)
npx serve -p 3000
```

**Open in Browser:**
```
http://localhost:3000
```

